+# FinBoom — Dashboard Action Links
+
+## Read-Only Forensic Analysis & Root-Cause Investigation
+
+You are working on the **FinBoom application repository**.
+
+We have identified a dashboard interaction issue involving five visible feature entry points. The UI renders the links/buttons correctly, but **clicking them produces no observable outcome**.
+
+### Important governance rule
+
+**THIS TASK IS READ-ONLY ANALYSIS ONLY.**
+
+Do **NOT** modify source code, tests, configuration, routes, package files, generated files, documentation, database/schema files, or any other repository artifact.
+
+Do **NOT**:
+
+* implement fixes;
+* add missing routes;
+* add click handlers;
+* create placeholder pages;
+* alter navigation;
+* change existing components;
+* install packages;
+* run formatters that modify files;
+* regenerate generated artifacts;
+* commit anything;
+* create a branch;
+* push anything.
+
+The objective is to establish the **exact root cause and implementation status** of these five dashboard entry points.
+
+---
+
+# 1. Issue Under Investigation
+
+The FinBoom dashboard currently displays:
+
+### A. Goals Progress
+
+Visible UI:
+
+* `GOALS PROGRESS`
+* `All ↗`
+* `No financial goals configured.`
+* `+ Set Financial Goal`
+
+Observed behavior:
+
+* Clicking **All ↗** produces no observable result.
+* Clicking **+ Set Financial Goal** produces no observable result.
+
+### B. Top Accounts
+
+Visible UI:
+
+* `TOP ACCOUNTS`
+* `View ↗`
+* `No accounts registered.`
+* `+ Link Account`
+
+Observed behavior:
+
+* Clicking **View ↗** produces no observable result.
+* Clicking **+ Link Account** produces no observable result.
+
+### C. Recent Transactions
+
+Visible UI:
+
+* `RECENT TRANSACTIONS`
+* `Ledger ↗`
+
+Observed behavior:
+
+* Clicking **Ledger ↗** produces no observable result.
+
+Therefore, there are currently five suspect dashboard entry points:
+
+| ID | UI element                       | Expected feature                |
+| -- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
+| D1 | Goals → `All ↗`                  | Financial Goals listing         |
+| D2 | `+ Set Financial Goal`           | Financial Goal creation         |
+| D3 | Top Accounts → `View ↗`          | Accounts view                   |
+| D4 | `+ Link Account`                 | Account linking/import workflow |
+| D5 | Recent Transactions → `Ledger ↗` | Transaction Ledger              |
+
+---
+
+# 2. Primary Objective
+
+Determine, with repository evidence, **why each of these five controls has no observable outcome**.
+
+Do not assume that the issue is a missing route.
+
+Determine which of the following applies to each control:
+
+1. No click handler exists.
+2. Click handler exists but does nothing.
+3. Navigation target is missing.
+4. Navigation target is incorrect.
+5. Route exists but is not registered.
+6. Route exists but component is missing/broken.
+7. Navigation uses an incorrect router/API.
+8. Feature exists elsewhere but dashboard integration is incomplete.
+9. Feature was intentionally deferred/not implemented.
+10. Feature belongs to another work package and has not yet been integrated.
+11. Feature is conditionally disabled.
+12. Authentication/authorization prevents navigation.
+13. Runtime JavaScript error prevents action.
+14. UI element is decorative/static despite looking actionable.
+15. Other — explain with evidence.
+
+For every conclusion, identify the exact repository evidence supporting it.
+
+---
+
+# 3. Start With Repository State
+
+Before investigating implementation:
+
+Capture, read-only:
+
+```text
+git status --short
+git branch --show-current
+git rev-parse HEAD
+git log -n 10 --oneline --decorate
+```
+
+Also determine:
+
+```text
+git remote -v
+```
+
+Do not change anything.
+
+Report the exact HEAD commit and working-tree state in the final analysis.
+
+---
+
+# 4. Locate the Dashboard Components
+
+Identify the exact source files responsible for rendering:
+
+* Goals Progress
+* Top Accounts
+* Recent Transactions
+
+Search the repository for distinctive UI strings, including:
+
+```text
+GOALS PROGRESS
+Set Financial Goal
+No financial goals configured
+TOP ACCOUNTS
+Link Account
+No accounts registered
+RECENT TRANSACTIONS
+Ledger
+```
+
+Do not rely only on filename guesses.
+
+For each match, establish:
+
+* file path;
+* component name;
+* parent component;
+* route/page where rendered;
+* relevant imports;
+* navigation mechanism;
+* event handlers;
+* feature flags or conditional rendering.
+
+Provide source-line references in the report.
+
+---
+
+# 5. Trace Each Interaction End-to-End
+
+Perform a separate forensic trace for each control.
+
+## D1 — Goals → All
+
+Determine:
+
+```text
+UI element
+    ↓
+component
+    ↓
+event/navigation handler
+    ↓
+target path / route / action
+    ↓
+router configuration
+    ↓
+destination component
+    ↓
+actual feature implementation
+```
+
+Report whether every link in this chain exists.
+
+---
+
+## D2 — Set Financial Goal
+
+Trace:
+
+```text
+"+ Set Financial Goal"
+    ↓
+button/link component
+    ↓
+onClick/navigation
+    ↓
+target
+    ↓
+route/modal/drawer/page
+    ↓
+goal creation UI
+    ↓
+goal persistence/service/API
+```
+
+Determine whether the goal-setting feature actually exists.
+
+Do not assume that because the dashboard says "Set Financial Goal", the goal feature has been implemented.
+
+---
+
+## D3 — Top Accounts → View
+
+Trace:
+
+```text
+"View ↗"
+    ↓
+Accounts dashboard control
+    ↓
+navigation
+    ↓
+target route
+    ↓
+accounts page/component
+    ↓
+account data layer
+```
+
+Determine whether an accounts destination exists and whether this dashboard control is correctly wired to it.
+
+---
+
+## D4 — Link Account
+
+Trace:
+
+```text
+"+ Link Account"
+    ↓
+button/link
+    ↓
+handler
+    ↓
+navigation/modal
+    ↓
+account linking/import workflow
+    ↓
+backend/API/service
+```
+
+Determine whether the account-linking workflow exists.
+
+Pay particular attention to any existing bank-account import/native-bank-import functionality or previous work packages that may already contain the intended destination.
+
+Do not implement or alter anything.
+
+---
+
+## D5 — Ledger
+
+Trace:
+
+```text
+"Ledger ↗"
+    ↓
+link/button
+    ↓
+navigation
+    ↓
+ledger route
+    ↓
+ledger component/page
+    ↓
+transaction data source
+```
+
+Determine whether the Ledger feature already exists and whether this dashboard link is correctly connected to it.
+
+---
+
+# 6. Search the Entire Repository for Existing Features
+
+Do not limit the investigation to the dashboard.
+
+Search for concepts and components related to:
+
+### Goals
+
+```text
+goal
+goals
+financial goal
+financial goals
+goal progress
+goal creation
+goal setting
+```
+
+### Accounts
+
+```text
+account
+accounts
+link account
+linked account
+bank account
+bank import
+account import
+```
+
+### Ledger
+
+```text
+ledger
+transactions
+transaction ledger
+transaction history
+```
+
+Identify:
+
+* existing pages;
+* routes;
+* components;
+* services;
+* APIs;
+* hooks;
+* state stores;
+* feature modules;
+* navigation definitions;
+* tests.
+
+The key question is:
+
+> **Does the underlying feature already exist somewhere in FinBoom but simply fail to connect from these dashboard controls?**
+
+---
+
+# 7. Router and Navigation Forensics
+
+Identify which routing/navigation technology FinBoom uses.
+
+Examples may include:
+
+```text
+React Router
+TanStack Router
+Next.js routing
+custom navigation
+window.location
+history API
+application navigation service
+```
+
+Then inspect:
+
+* route definitions;
+* route registration;
+* route guards;
+* lazy-loaded routes;
+* navigation helpers;
+* sidebar/header navigation;
+* existing links to the same destinations.
+
+Look for an existing working navigation path to each suspected destination.
+
+For example:
+
+If Ledger is already accessible from another part of the application, compare the working navigation implementation with the dashboard `Ledger ↗` implementation.
+
+Do the same for Goals and Accounts.
+
+---
+
+# 8. Browser/Runtime Investigation
+
+If a local development environment is available, perform **observation only**.
+
+Do not modify files.
+
+For each of the five controls:
+
+1. Open the relevant dashboard.
+2. Click the control.
+3. Observe URL/location.
+4. Observe visible UI.
+5. Observe browser console.
+6. Observe network activity if relevant.
+7. Check whether a JavaScript exception occurs.
+8. Determine whether the click event fires.
+9. Determine whether navigation is attempted.
+
+Capture concise evidence.
+
+If browser tooling is unavailable, explicitly state that and continue with static repository forensics.
+
+Do not claim runtime behavior that you did not actually observe.
+
+---
+
+# 9. Compare Against Existing Working Navigation
+
+Search for any existing working links/buttons that lead to:
+
+* Goals
+* Accounts
+* Account linking/import
+* Ledger/Transactions
+
+If working equivalents exist, compare:
+
+```text
+dashboard implementation
+vs.
+working implementation
+```
+
+Identify differences in:
+
+* route path;
+* router API;
+* component;
+* event handler;
+* permissions;
+* feature flag;
+* navigation helper;
+* query parameters;
+* state requirements.
+
+---
+
+# 10. Git History / Work Package Investigation
+
+Use git history **read-only** to determine when these dashboard controls were introduced.
+
+For relevant files/components, inspect:
+
+```text
+git log --follow -- <file>
+git blame <file>
+```
+
+Use targeted searches such as:
+
+```text
+git log --all --oneline --grep="goal"
+git log --all --oneline --grep="account"
+git log --all --oneline --grep="ledger"
+```
+
+Also inspect relevant commits where appropriate.
+
+Determine:
+
+* Which work package introduced each UI element?
+* Was the corresponding feature supposed to be delivered in the same work package?
+* Was navigation explicitly deferred?
+* Is there evidence that the dashboard UI was added ahead of the destination implementation?
+* Is there evidence of a regression?
+
+Do not infer work-package ownership without evidence.
+
+---
+
+# 11. Tests
+
+Locate tests associated with:
+
+* dashboard;
+* goals;
+* accounts;
+* account linking/import;
+* ledger;
+* navigation.
+
+Determine whether tests cover:
+
+```text
+rendering
+click behavior
+navigation
+destination rendering
+feature availability
+```
+
+Pay special attention to cases where a component test verifies that a button exists but does **not** verify that clicking it produces the expected result.
+
+Report any such testing gap.
+
+Do not modify tests.
+
+---
+
+# 12. Distinguish UI Presence From Feature Completion
+
+This distinction is mandatory.
+
+For every feature, separately classify:
+
+### Layer 1 — Visual presence
+
+Does the dashboard control render?
+
+### Layer 2 — Interaction wiring
+
+Does clicking it invoke an action?
+
+### Layer 3 — Navigation/action target
+
+Does the action lead somewhere meaningful?
+
+### Layer 4 — Destination implementation
+
+Does the destination feature actually exist?
+
+### Layer 5 — Functional workflow
+
+Does the underlying workflow operate?
+
+### Layer 6 — Persistence/integration
+
+Where applicable, does it integrate with the correct backend/data layer?
+
+Do not mark a feature "complete" merely because Layer 1 exists.
+
+---
+
+# 13. Required Evidence Matrix
+
+Produce this exact type of matrix:
+
+| ID | Control            | Rendered | Handler | Target | Route Exists | Destination Exists | Runtime Result | Root Cause | Status |
+| -- | ------------------ | -------: | ------: | ------ | -----------: | -----------------: | -------------- | ---------- | ------ |
+| D1 | Goals → All        |          |         |        |              |                    |                |            |        |
+| D2 | Set Financial Goal |          |         |        |              |                    |                |            |        |
+| D3 | Accounts → View    |          |         |        |              |                    |                |            |        |
+| D4 | Link Account       |          |         |        |              |                    |                |            |        |
+| D5 | Ledger             |          |         |        |              |                    |                |            |        |
+
+Use:
+
+* `YES`
+* `NO`
+* `N/A`
+* `UNKNOWN`
+
+Do not use assumptions to fill the matrix.
+
+---
+
+# 14. Root-Cause Classification
+
+For each D1–D5, provide one primary classification:
+
+```text
+RC-01 — Missing event handler
+RC-02 — Handler exists but is inert
+RC-03 — Missing navigation target
+RC-04 — Incorrect navigation target
+RC-05 — Route not registered
+RC-06 — Destination component missing
+RC-07 — Existing feature not integrated into dashboard
+RC-08 — Runtime exception
+RC-09 — Auth/permission issue
+RC-10 — Feature intentionally deferred
+RC-11 — Feature belongs to another pending work package
+RC-12 — Regression
+RC-13 — Other
+```
+
+If multiple causes exist, identify:
+
+* primary root cause;
+* contributing cause(s).
+
+---
+
+# 15. Severity Assessment
+
+Classify each issue:
+
+### P0
+
+Application fundamentally unusable.
+
+### P1
+
+Core promised feature inaccessible from a primary dashboard workflow.
+
+### P2
+
+Feature exists but dashboard integration/navigation is broken.
+
+### P3
+
+Minor navigation/UX issue with an accessible alternative.
+
+Explain the reasoning.
+
+---
+
+# 16. Do Not Fix Yet
+
+This investigation must end with a **diagnosis**, not an implementation.
+
+Do NOT:
+
+* edit code;
+* create routes;
+* wire handlers;
+* create pages;
+* modify tests;
+* modify package configuration;
+* commit changes.
+
+If a fix is clearly required, describe the required implementation at a design level only.
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+D5 — Ledger
+
+Required implementation:
+Connect the dashboard Ledger control to the existing Ledger route
+<identified route>, using the same navigation mechanism currently
+used by <identified working control>.
+
+No code changes performed during this investigation.
+```
+
+---
+
+# 17. Final Report Structure
+
+Return a concise but evidence-rich report with exactly these sections:
+
+## 1. Repository State
+
+Include:
+
+* branch;
+* HEAD;
+* working tree;
+* relevant recent commits.
+
+## 2. Executive Finding
+
